  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>At LATYS Intelligence Inc. (“LATYS,” “we,” “us,” or “our”), we use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your experience on our website. This Cookie Policy explains what cookies are, how we use them, and your options regarding their use.</p>
  <p>latysfocus.com is a product website operated by LATYS Intelligence Inc., which also operates latys.ca. Both websites are subject to the same data practices and policies of LATYS Intelligence Inc.</p>
  <p>This Cookie Policy supplements our Privacy Policy, available at latys.ca/privacy, which describes more broadly how we collect, use, and protect your personal information.</p>

  <h2>2. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small text files that are placed on your device (computer, smartphone, tablet) when you visit our website. They help us recognize your device and store some information about your preferences or past actions on the site.</p>
  <p>There are different types of cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Session Cookies:</strong> Temporary cookies that expire once you close your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Persistent Cookies:</strong> Remain on your device until deleted or until they reach their expiration date.</li>
    <li><strong>First-Party Cookies:</strong> Set by the website you are visiting.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-Party Cookies:</strong> Set by other services or platforms (e.g., analytics, advertising networks).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How LATYS Uses Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use cookies for several purposes, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Necessary for the proper functioning of the website. Without them, certain features may not work. These cookies do not require consent and cannot be disabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Performance and Analytics Cookies:</strong> Help us understand how visitors interact with our website, such as pages visited and time spent on the site. We use tools like Google Analytics to gather this data. These cookies are only set after you provide consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Functionality Cookies:</strong> Allow us to remember your preferences (e.g., language or location) to provide a more personalized experience. These cookies are only set after you provide consent, unless strictly necessary for the site to function.</li>
    <li><strong>Targeting or Advertising Cookies:</strong> Track your browsing habits so we can show you relevant advertisements or limit the number of times you see a particular ad. These cookies are only set after you provide consent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>We may also use third-party cookies on our website for services such as analytics, social media integration, and advertising. These third parties have their own privacy and cookie policies, which we recommend reviewing:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Analytics: Google’s Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/policy.php">Meta/Facebook Ads: Meta’s Privacy Policy</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>These third-party cookies are not loaded until you have given consent via our cookie settings banner. We do not have control over how these third parties process data once collected, but we take reasonable steps to select providers with appropriate privacy practices.</p>

  <h2>5. Managing Your Cookie Preferences</h2>
  <p>You have the right to accept or reject non-essential cookies. Under Québec Law 25, non-essential cookies are not placed on your device until you provide consent.</p>
  <p><strong>Cookie Banner:</strong> When you first visit our website, you will see a cookie banner that allows you to accept or decline non-essential cookies (analytics, functionality, and advertising cookies). You can change your preferences at any time by adjusting your cookie settings via the banner or the cookie preferences link in the website footer.</p>
  <p><strong>Browser Settings:</strong> You can also modify your browser settings to block or delete cookies. Each browser is different, but cookie management options are typically found in your browser’s “Settings” or “Privacy” section. Please note that if you disable cookies through your browser, some features of our website may not function properly.</p>

  <h2>6. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>
  <p>LATYS reserves the right to update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our use of cookies or applicable law. We will post any changes on this page and update the “Last Updated” date at the top of the policy.</p>

  <h2>7. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Cookie Policy, please contact us at:</p>
  <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:info@latys.ca">info@latys.ca</a><br /><strong>Address:</strong> 321 Rue de la Commune West, Suite 300, Montréal, Québec H2Y 2E1, Canada</p>
  <p>For questions regarding your broader privacy rights, please see our Privacy Policy at latys.ca/privacy or contact our Privacy Officer at <a href="mailto:info@latys.ca">info@latys.ca</a>.</p>
